WEBVTT

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.650
Hey!

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.400
Aoki-san!

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.290
It’s been a while!

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.660
What’ve you been doing for the past week?

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.460
So this jackass finally shows his face around here.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.040
Have you recovered?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.670
Gee whiz, I’m starting to blush here.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.550
It’s great getting this warm reception, but...

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.780
"But"?

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.760
Are you...?

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.340
No way!

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.340
I see. So you’re retiring.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.630
Thanks for everything!

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.100
You’ve done good.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.840
At least that was my original plan.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.980
Good evening.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.950
Uh, nice to meet you!

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.360
I can’t hear you! Shape up, will you?

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.640
W-We were very moved by Aoki-sensei’s{lol, Kodomo no Jikan reference} match!

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.370
So we took the next step and decided to put ourselves under his wing!

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.590
"S-Sensei"?

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.350
That would mean I’m the hero.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.490
That means I got charisma.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.980
I’ve given them hope.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.380
I’ve given them a dream.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.270
So for their sakes, I ain’t gonna do it.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.430
I ain’t gonna retire.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.190
So that means we got us more gofers.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.750
That’s great, ‘cause I could <i>go for</i>  some juice.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.080
W-We're here for Aoki.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.150
So...

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:31.940
Go get it for him.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.290
Yessir!

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.900
<i>They only listen to Aoki-san?</i>

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.160
<i>They actually ignored Takamura-san?</i>

00:01:42.460 --> 00:02:05.190
Sendou! Sendou! Sendou!{ad infinitum}

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.060
<i>S-So many people cheering for him.</i>

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.000
<i>This  </i>is <i>Sendou-san’s comeback fight.</i>

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.110
Holy smokes! He’s still down!

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.460
No count needed here!

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.300
That’s the match!

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.260
It sure as heck didn't look like he came back from anything!

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.880
But Sendou Takeshi is back!

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.950
The Naniwa Tiger is now reborn!

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:45.770
Here it is!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.550
<i>He must be happy about that win.</i>

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.190
Are you crazy?!

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.030
You saying you got a problem with my match?

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.870
Wh-What was that? He doesn’t seem happy at all.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.190
Oh, is that you, Makunouchi-kun?

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.880
G-Good evening!

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.670
We’re actually a little busy.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.670
Oh, Sendou! It’s Makunouchi-kun!

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.670
Ah, Makunouchi! You came!

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.150
Congratulations! You were amazing!

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.370
You’re damn right I was amazing!

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.710
So would you mind telling <i>him</i>  that?

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.890
Who?

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.190
That’s Sawamura from Nagano. 
He was my sparring partner.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.280
<i>Sawamura from Nagoya?</i>

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.900
<i>He’s the third-ranked fighter in the Japanese featherweight division.</i>

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.490
Sawamura Ryuuhei.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:43.000
I thought I’d meet you in the ring during our title match, Champion.

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.950
H-How are you?

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:50.970
U-Um...

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.240
I won’t shake hands.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.970
I don’t wish to sympathize with those I take the belt from.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.860
I-Is that so?

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.180
I guess that <i>would</i>  be a concern.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.710
Later.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.480
Yeah, get lost!

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.080
Can you believe his attitude?

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.470
Don’cha wanna beat him black and blue?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:10.980
Nah!

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.740
Oh. Can you do me a favor, Champion?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.660
Yes!

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.580
Yeah?

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.220
You know that Dempsey Roll of yours?

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.300
Do not use it when we fight.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.540
That pathetic little move will be utterly pulverized.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.170
<i>Pathetic?</i>

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:39.450
I hate to say it, but the guy's the real deal.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.120
He even put me out in a few sparring sessions.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.060
He was here to criticize my game.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.770
He thinks my timing was off.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.010
Timing?

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:55.740
So you figured it out, huh?

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.490
That’s right. Counters are the Dempsey Roll’s weakness.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.240
You better be careful out there, Makunouchi.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.480
The guy's a prodigy when it comes to counters.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.500
Maybe an even bigger prodigy than that Miyata Ichirou.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.190
M-Miyata-kun?

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.220
You’re kidding.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.050
You can call him...

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.250
the Dempsey Roll’s archenemy!

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.950
<i>The Dempsey Roll is pathetic?</i>

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.260
<i>That’s pretty maddening.</i>

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.110
<i>Sawamura Ryuuhei-san, was it?</i>

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.500
<i>I want to beat him with my Dempsey Roll.</i>

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.510
We would now like to hear some comments.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.900
We’ll start with the challenger, Larry Bernard-san.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:06:00.930
I’m not a boxer who relies on cheap tricks. I’m a purebred fighter!

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:04.610
I really look forward to the champion fighting me head on instead of juking around.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:09.040
That way, I’ll give you a slugfest you’ll be telling your grandkids about!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.260
I’d say he’s confident.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.800
So he’s saying he’s taking Takamura head on?

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.630
May we have a word from the champion?

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.450
I have an important announcement to make.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.940
I am leaving the junior middleweight class as of now.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.370
That means I’ll be giving up my belt.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.700
I'll conquer the middleweights, the super middleweights,

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.770
then the heavyweight division!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.920
I'll be the first to sweep all six divisions!

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.260
But all of that is just mere talk.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:48.930
First, I need to put this guy through a bloodbath before you people can believe me.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.770
He will not land a punch on me!

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.690
The only one punching will be me!

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.700
Are you sure about this, Takamura-san?

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:10.900
You really pissed off the challenger.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.210
He says he <i>will</i>  land a punch on you.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.750
No need to worry, pipsqueaks.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.740
I have a strategy!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:27.650
We will now conduct the world junior middleweight title match!

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.700
I wonder what his strategy is.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.020
Not sure. We'll just have to wait and see.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:34.980
The smell!

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.060
I can smell it!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.520
Smell what?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.750
I can smell it clearly!

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:44.030
The sweet smell of winning without even trying!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.030
<i>He made me lose face!</i>

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.040
<i>Now, I’m gonna shut up that big mouth of his!</i>

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:57.090
<i>I can’t waste time here, not with the six-division sweep waiting.</i>

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.000
<i>I’ll make quick work of him.</i>

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.710
<i>You’re dead!</i>

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:03.650
Box!

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.220
That’s the bell!

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.300
Both fighters approach each other in the center.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.970
They both raise their fists toward each other...

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:14.160
Whoa! The challenger brushes off the other fist!

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.930
He just couldn't hide his emotions!

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.190
<i>I’ll kill you!</i>

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.650
<i>You little pup.</i>

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.980
<i>I saw your plan from a mile away!</i>

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.740
<i>Take a...</i>

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.840
<i>look at this!</i>

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.620
It... It’s the Look-Away!

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:32.120
That’s my move!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.770
<i>All I’m doing now is copying Aoki.</i>

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.380
<i>But I’m nothing like that pipsqueak.</i>

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.870
<i>So I’m gonna...</i>

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.230
<i>do this!</i>

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:46.000
Holy Toledo! The champion turned his entire body!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.630
What’s going on here?

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:51.090
<i>So did you fall for it, Mr. Clean?</i>

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.430
<i>You’re wondering what I’m looking at, aren’t you?</i>

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.610
You moron! Don’t look away!

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.140
Takamura-kun, look back!

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.040
You’re only supposed to look for a second!

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.780
You’re taking too long!

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:02.650
Eyes in front!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.900
Whoa! He makes good on his promise of one punch!

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.830
And what a punch it is, folks!

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:24.730
He really felt that!

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.000
Get a hold of yourself!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.430
Open your eyes!

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.340
Takamura-kun!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:31.390
He’s right in front of you!

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:33.850
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.740
<i>Why? That move fooled me 100% of the time!</i>

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.390
<i>Why didn’t it fool him?</i>

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:42.580
The champion’s now looking grim!

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:43.930
It must've been from that punch!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.320
Now the challenger is punching from left and right!

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.320
The champion is pinned at the corner!

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.210
Look out!

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:49.900
He’ll kill you!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.820
Don’t get KO’d!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.050
The punches keep coming!

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.240
B-But what’s happening?

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.560
H-He’s dodging every one.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.000
<i>I've had just about enough of your...</i>

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.420
<i>crap!</i>

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.250
The challenger plows through 
the mat with a sickening thud!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.430
The referee rushes over! Will there be a count?

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:23.940
Nope! That’s the end of the match!

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.150
That’s pretty much...

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.190
what I’m talking about!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.910
Screw off! You took a hit!

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.690
You liar!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.130
Don’t scare us like that!

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.210
Don’t throw items toward the ring!

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.210
You ain't sweeping six divisions!

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.270
Please, do not throw items toward the ring!

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:43.430
It’s <i>your</i>  fault I embarrassed myself out there!

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:46.250
Run! He’ll kill you!

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.480
You’re <i>really</i>  taking it out on him?

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.760
It wasn’t his fault at all.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.460
That was absolutely, positively pathetic!

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.300
Why can’t you <i>ever</i>  do things right?!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.270
Are you even aware that you’re the world champ?!

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.650
I won, so quit whining!

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.980
And this is the last junior middleweight fight I’m doing!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.930
Get ready for my next division sweep!

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:13.400
I’m not done talking to you!

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:20.570
If he stuck with the junior middleweights, he’d keep defending his title and get rich off the purses.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.670
I know it’s tough maintaining weight, but he didn’t have to give up his belt just like that.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.900
You think... he did that in haste?

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.420
I never thought of it that way.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:37.950
He’s a guy who lives for the limelight, so as long as he shows off his physical prowess, he's good.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.080
That man has no real use for money or possessions.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.100
Take a look.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.670
Now who would ever forget that?

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.650
That’s just like Takamura-san.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:52.140
<i>It’s just like Takamura-san to forget this,</i>

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:55.200
<i>as it is just like Takamura-san to go for a six-division sweep.</i>

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:00.090
<i>He’ll become a boxer that commands the world’s attention, and not just the nation’s.</i>

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.910
<i>That’s what I think.</i>

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.580
<i>And it  </i>will <i>happen soon.</i>

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:14.210
So, how many times have you defended your title since becoming the Japanese champion?

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.180
F-Four times.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.220
Only a fine champion can successfully defend four times.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.710
I think it’s now time to think about the next step.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:25.680
However...

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:31.860
Do you know what all these challenges mean?

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:34.130
F-Four of them?

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:37.110
They all think my belt is easy pickings?

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:39.870
You’re a cheese champion.

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:41.210
Cheese?

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:45.690
You’re a champion full of holes, just like Swiss cheese.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:48.370
I-I sound delicious, don’t I?

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.750
These are proof of how little the other boxers think of you.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:56.130
If you’re going to rise up, we must believe there's no one in Japan who's capable of beating you.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:58.930
Choose.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:02.410
Choose from these four challengers.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:04.640
I-I’m supposed to decide?

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:06.650
Are you sure?

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.200
If I could,

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:20.910
I would like to fight him.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.650
<i>Sawamura Ryuuhei?</i>

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.120
Let me fight him.

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:37.700
Please!

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:50.810
Are you really sure about putting him up against Sawamura Ryuuhei?

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:54.550
Did you see the look on his face?

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:57.280
I’ve rarely seen him that assertive.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:01.180
There's no one alive who would say he’s a prideful man.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:03.530
Yet he looked determined.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:07.100
I’m putting my money on his disposition as a man.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:13.540
Even if he loses, I hope he uses that as a springboard to develop even more.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.290
Loses?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.800
Is his foe that formidable?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.300
He is.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:26.050
I’m sure the kid is turning pale looking at the videos.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:31.330
I-It can’t be...

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:35.520
What is this counter?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.570
Sorry for making you all come over.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.550
The video is who Ippo’s up against next.

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:50.320
But I ain’t well versed in pipsqueak boxers.

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:53.080
So I needed you guys to take a look.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:06.700
He’s using Shimabukuro as a punching bag!

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:11.350
So the one other guy he lost to was Sawamura?!

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:15.850
But it still came down to a decision despite the beating he took?

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:20.280
Shimabukuro-san looks so disappointed.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.530
He could have KO’d him at any time, yet he decided to spare him.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:28.430
He knocked him down in the third round and again in the fourth,

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:30.790
but he didn’t take him out of his misery after that.

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:34.540
That guy was clearly toying with him!

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.040
This is very humiliating.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.050
But he <i>is</i>  very talented.

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:43.930
There!

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:49.180
A normal counter is often done <i>after</i>  the opponent punches, but he does it <i>before</i>  the punch.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:53.560
He had the intuitiveness and the lightning- fast arm speed to perform that feat.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.640
Yeah.

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:56.730
He’s not like Miyata-kun.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.310
This is completely different.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.500
Miyata throws himself into his opponents’ punches and hits back.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:06.310
It’s like he’s throwing his entire soul...

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:09.320
into performing counters that glow like masterpieces.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:15.870
H-He’s right.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:20.280
Sawamura’s counters don’t glow, they’re just gloomy.

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:22.380
There's something very dark about them.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.330
I’m sick of this!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.510
Ain’t there a match where he gets hit?

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.880
Something to cleanse my palate.

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:31.390
Someone <i>managed</i>  to hit him.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.210
He got an elbow in!

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:39.770
Hell yeah, take him out!

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.340
Hey, don’t apologize!

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.820
It wasn’t on purpose, keep going!

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.640
Whoa!

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.040
Are you kidding?

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:05.710
This was a loss by foul.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:12.050
He later said, nonchalantly I might add, that he took "an eye for an eye."

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.660
Fujii-san. Iimura-san.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:19.060
Who’d thought Takamura-kun would invite me over to watch Sawamura videos?

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:21.910
Wh-What kind of person is he?

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:23.820
Sawamura Ryuuhei.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:27.150
He has a 9-2 record and four KO's.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.960
Both of his losses were caused by the same foul.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:34.640
And just as you guessed, his lack of KO's is due to him playing with his preys.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.730
His moral turpitude doesn’t stop at the ring.

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:41.340
Whether it’s at a train station or a dark street corner,

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:46.590
he will hurt anyone who bumps his shoulders or pisses him off in general.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:52.080
He avoided total banishment because his own gym decided to suspend him.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:56.270
H-He’s attacking ordinary people even though he’s a pro boxer?

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.650
Takamura-san, what do you think?

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:01.220
You’ve been silent this whole time.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.760
I’ve been meaning to say this for a while...

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.400
It's too crowded in here!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.020
How many people came anyway?!

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:14.870
Dumbasses!

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:27.570
P... Please let us go!

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:29.710
What did we ever do to you?!

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.490
Nothing.

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:34.760
I just wanted you gone.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:38.760
I-I know you! You’re a pro boxer, right?!

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.690
We’ll run to the police if you don’t stop!

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.770
Then you won’t be able to box at all!

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.020
I-I’ll really press char—

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:02.290
Press charges?

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.630
Maybe if you can still talk.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:16.820
Sawamura!

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.800
How the hell did you injure your hand?!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.750
Don’t tell me you fought someone again!

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:26.560
Coach. I'm not an idiot.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:28.750
S-So you didn’t fight anyone?

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:33.400
Let me see that. A fist is a boxer’s life, you know.

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.410
Wh-What's with these teeth marks?!

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:41.120
Did you send Makunouchi the challenge?

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:42.300
Y-Yeah.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.000
We’re expecting a reply anytime soon.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.330
But still, these teeth marks...

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.620
I can’t wait to fight in a title match.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.760
I repeat: I'm not an idiot.

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:57.930
If there <i>were</i>  any problems...

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:02.450
I would wipe them out myself.
